  [OK] P6a *** a0(z)/a0(0) IS EXACTLY kappa-BLIND, symbolically: d/dkappa = 0 and kappa does not appear in the ratio (z + 1)**(3*w_0/2 + 3*w_a/2 + 3/2)*exp(-3*w_a*z/(2*(z + 1))). *** So F5 contributes ZERO information about kappa no matter how good the data get. It constrains (w0, wa) and the FLOOR TYPE -- and it brings (w0,wa) with it, so in the dof ledger it is net-zero, not a free constraint
  a0(z)/a0(0) = (z + 1)**(3*w_0/2 + 3*w_a/2 + 3/2)*exp(-3*w_a*z/(2*(z + 1)))   (the committed closed form: bump-then-decline for wa < 0)
