  [OK] P8e *** AND THE DECISIVE ANSWER IS NO: kappa = 1/2 IS NOT UNIQUE. *** 3 of the 5 tested kappa values survive the joint at <= 2 sigma-equivalent (kappa = 1/2pi, kappa = 1/2, kappa = 1/2, ALT footing). Adding F2-F5 to F1 does NOT sharpen F1's 2.2-sigma preference into a unique value, because the fronts that could sharpen it are the ones that do not bind (F3, F5) or that bind in the WRONG DIRECTION (F4 wants 6.7x, F2b caps at 1.49x). Outcome (c), a CONTINUUM in kappa

