  [OK] P8-ORDER *** AND THE JOINT DOES NOT EVEN PRESERVE THE ORDERING. *** Delta chi2 between kappa = 1/2pi and kappa = 1/2, each at its own most favourable cell, is -0.585 -- inside the 2.71 that a 90%-confidence one-parameter separation would need, i.e. the two coefficients are statistically INDISTINGUISHABLE in the joint. P2d(i) reproduced the committed 2.2 sigma AT FIXED alpha=1; P2d(ii) showed it reverses when the kernel is freed; here the two effects cancel to nothing. Honest reading: F1's kappa discrimination is real ONLY conditional on the alpha=1 kernel, and the alpha=1 kernel is the one P3/P8b exclude at 378 sigma. The 2.2-sigma claim therefore cannot be quoted as a joint result without that condition attached

